repository-code: "https://github.com/TiredofSleep/trinity-infinity-geometry"
url: "https://github.com/TiredofSleep/trinity-infinity-geometry"
abstract: >-
  Research extending the premise of the book "The Shape of Understanding":
  an integer n is read as a configuration of n points, and one asks what
  shape the configuration is forced to take. The integers 0-4 are forced by
  equal distance (the void, point, segment, triangle, tetrahedron); the
  tetrahedron fixes the number 1/3 (cos of its angle is -1/3); the cube is
  the perpendicular build, 2^3 corners, two tetrahedra, and carries the
  Clifford algebra Cl(3). Beyond four points the natural rules part ways:
  spreading points on a sphere forces the octahedron at 6 but not the
  pentagon at 5 or the cube at 8, and 7 and 9 are not yet realized by a
  single rule. Every forced claim is machine-checked by short numpy scripts.
  An earlier table-based program is archived at the tag archive-2026-09-24.
keywords:
